=You are writing a short daily note about the health of an IBM Quantum processor for the engineer who owns it.

Today's run on {{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.backend }}:
- Qubit pair q{{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.controlQubit }} and q{{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.targetQubit }}, chosen automatically as the lowest-error linked pair out of {{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.linksEvaluated }} candidates
- Measured correlation: {{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.correlationScore }} (share of shots landing on 00 or 11 for a Bell pair, 1.0 would be perfect)
- Correlation predicted from calibration data: {{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.predictedCorrelation }}
- CZ gate error {{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.czError }}, readout errors {{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.readoutErrorControl }} and {{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.readoutErrorTarget }}
- T1 {{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.t1Control }} and {{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.t1Target }} microseconds, T2 {{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.t2Control }} and {{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.t2Target }} microseconds
- Calibration last refreshed at {{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.calibrationUpdatedAt }}, queue depth at submit {{ $('Calculate Correlation Score').item.json.queueLength }}

Recent history: {{ $json.historyCount }} scored runs, mean {{ $json.rollingMean }}, best {{ $json.bestScore }}, worst {{ $json.worstScore }}, today sits {{ $json.deltaVsRollingMean }} away from the mean. Each history line lists its own backend and qubit pair, so check them before blaming a change of pair.
{{ $json.historyTable }}

Write three to five sentences of plain prose. No headings, no bullet points, no markdown. State whether today reads as normal, better or worse than the recent trend. If something is off, name the most likely cause among readout drift, two-qubit gate degradation, a fresh recalibration, or a change of backend or qubit pair. Only mention a change of pair or backend if the history lines actually show a different one from today; if the pair is unchanged, say so and look elsewhere. A persistent gap between measured and predicted correlation means the calibration numbers are optimistic for this link, which is itself worth reporting. Finish with one concrete suggestion. Never invent numbers that are not listed above.
